  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # find rows and columns that contain at least one 1\n    rows_with_one = [r for r in range(rows) if any(grid[r][c] == 1 for c in range(cols))]\n    cols_with_one = [c for c in range(cols) if any(grid[r][c] == 1 for r in range(rows))]\n    \n    if not rows_with_one or not cols_with_one:\n        return grid\n    \n    top = min(rows_with_one)\n    bottom = max(rows_with_one)\n    left = min(cols_with_one)\n    right = max(cols_with_one)\n    \n    # make a copy to avoid modifying input while reading\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # helper to set 2 if cell is 0\n    def fill(r, c):\n        if out[r][c] == 0:\n            out[r][c] = 2\n    \n    # Process rows\n    for r in range(rows):\n        ones = [c for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == 1]\n        if len(ones) < 2:\n            continue\n        for i in range(len(ones)-1):\n            c1 = ones[i]\n            c2 = ones[i+1]\n            if r == top or r == bottom:\n                # fill whole interval\n                for c in range(c1+1, c2):\n                    fill(r, c)\n            else:\n                # interior row: fill only if gap is exactly one cell\n                if c2 == c1 + 2:\n                    fill(r, c1+1)\n    \n    # Process columns\n    for c in range(cols):\n        ones = [r for r in range(rows) if grid[r][c] == 1]\n        if len(ones) < 2:\n            continue\n        for i in range(len(ones)-1):\n            r1 = ones[i]\n            r2 = ones[i+1]\n            if c == left or c == right:\n                for r in range(r1+1, r2):\n                    fill(r, c)\n            else:\n                if r2 == r1 + 2:\n                    fill(r1+1, c)\n    \n    return out\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # find rows and columns that contain at least one 1\n    rows_with_one = [r for r in range(rows) if any(grid[r][c] == 1 for c in range(cols))]\n    cols_with_one = [c for c in range(cols) if any(grid[r][c] == 1 for r in range(rows))]\n    \n    if not rows_with_one or not cols_with_one:\n        return grid\n    \n    top = min(rows_with_one)\n    bottom = max(rows_with_one)\n    left = min(cols_with_one)\n    right = max(cols_with_one)\n    \n    # make a copy to avoid modifying input while reading\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # helper to set 2 if cell is 0\n    def fill(r, c):\n        if out[r][c] == 0:\n            out[r][c] = 2\n    \n    # Process rows\n    for r in range(rows):\n        ones = [c for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == 1]\n        if len(ones) < 2:\n            continue\n        for i in range(len(ones)-1):\n            c1 = ones[i]\n            c2 = ones[i+1]\n            if r == top or r == bottom:\n                # fill whole interval\n                for c in range(c1+1, c2):\n                    fill(r, c)\n            else:\n                # interior row: fill only if gap is exactly one cell\n                if c2 == c1 + 2:\n                    fill(r, c1+1)\n    \n    # Process columns\n    for c in range(cols):\n        ones = [r for r in range(rows) if grid[r][c] == 1]\n        if len(ones) < 2:\n            continue\n        for i in range(len(ones)-1):\n            r1 = ones[i]\n            r2 = ones[i+1]\n            if c == left or c == right:\n                for r in range(r1+1, r2):\n                    fill(r, c)\n            else:\n                if r2 == r1 + 2:\n                    fill(r1+1, c)\n    \n    return out",
